{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/771820-doors-in-the-pen-umbra","id":771820,"title":"Doors in the (Pen)Umbra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-22T16:16:37-08:00","id":771820,"title":"Doors in the (Pen)Umbra","content":"Ok, it appeared to our group yesterday that most of us seem to have heard about some rule, but research can't pin it down. The &quot;rule&quot; in question is, that doors in the Penumbra can't be opened. Our GM said, she heard about it long ago, but thought it was just something her former GM made up, one of the players said, that he had always played with this rule and even could provide what they had used for crossing through them (doors don't change state in the Umbra, but you could cross them with gnosis vs. 8 if closed, because they could be opened in the Tellurian).<br /> <br /> As a result I checked the W20 core book and W20 Umbra, but couldn't find any evidence for this, only that you could destroy the umbral reflection and as a result destroy the real object within an unspecified time (W20 p 317)<br /> <br /> So, I would like to ask if any of you could find any proof or falsification of this rule, which might, or might not be hidden somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T17:22:09-08:00","id":771914,"title":"","content":"I've never heard that before. If it's a home rule I guess it's fine, but otherwise you can just ask them to provide a book and page number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T19:10:07-08:00","id":771993,"title":"","content":"Even if that's the house rule that's being gone with, I think there was a mechanic for rolling and/or spending Gnosis to alter the environment. So if you needed to get through a wall in the Umbra, you could move around the pattern with your own essence to make a path. I don't recall if this was purely a house rule of games I was in or was explicitly stated in the books also, but this was supposedly a less invasive way to do things, also - because the damage to the pattern was more likely to be mended without fuss, rather than cause degradation to the physical side, and so in turn was less likely to piss off Weaver spirits.<br /> <br /> I don't remember if this is a thing in W20 also, sounds like it has been dropped, but it should be in previous editions. Sorry I can't offer a specific book or page number to go with it, I don't have those things handy to look them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T23:38:13-08:00","id":772118,"title":"","content":"I have read all the Umbral Books (Werewolf, Mage, Changelling, KoTE and Wraith) but never encountered that doors cannot be oppened and if you can't, there is always a way.<br /> As a home rule is very curious, if your GM apply that, well, is her game: the Master says, the gamer obbey.<br /> I got some and my players don't have a say in that, I informed before of it's use, so no probs with them.<br /> It's not a bad rule per se, she has do nothign wrong, really, if you don't like it, talk with her about it but if she don't want to change it, well, she's not gonna do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nosolorol.com/nuevo/images/Fostern.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1192-aura","name":"Aura","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T00:43:17-08:00","id":772145,"title":"","content":"I think i would rule that you can open doors in the penumbra. The denser the pattern web in the area is the more likly it won't be easy. If walking through a building where doors are unlocked then just pushing them will open them. <br /> If the door is usually locked it is likly locked in the umbra as well. You could smash the door down hoping that a pattern spider isn't watchng over it. If destroyed in the umbra then there will be a side effect in the real world with the door suddenly gaining cracks or warping. Alternatively a crafty Garou could get the spirit of the lock to open up with bribery, threats or other methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","name":"Cptmachine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T00:51:37-08:00","id":772149,"title":"","content":"If a door does not open, is it a door?<br /> <br /> But enough of that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> the posts above about using gnosis to open a door, or gifts (or even some spirit charms which do allow spirits to affect umbral walls and doors) do lead, and I agree with them, to that umbral doors could be used.<br /> <br /> I wonder if perhaps in a game an umbrally reflected door was protected, warded or guarded in some manner and it became a default understanding. Or perhaps as some spirits need charms to open them, that a belief was conjured that they were not accessible as some one from a physical reality of life would expect. <br /> <br /> Although now I am intrigued, skimming through books I dont see anything that says you universally cant affect umbrally reflected doors. if anyone does find anything, please do share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T06:56:21-08:00","id":772268,"title":"","content":"Man, what building are you in that even has doors in the penumbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T07:56:01-08:00","id":772305,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> IIRC, there are door(way)s into the Umbra which can be opened, but the person wanting to go through cannot because the realm it leads to is off limits for him/her. Some realms can only be walked into by specific types of people, e.g. Garou, Mages, some Vampires and Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T08:03:49-08:00","id":772311,"title":"","content":"The question is about doors in an umbral building. Yes there are certain realms with gates/tors/doors/portals take your pick that can only be opened by insert splat here. <br /> Now as to the OP's question I think this rule was in the 2nd edition core. I don't have a hard copy and have not download it to my phone. I also thought it was an optional rule that only applied in high gauntlet facilities like science labs and nuclear facilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T08:47:15-08:00","id":772340,"title":"","content":"2nd Ed core? Let me see...<br /> <br /> Ahhh, Pages 26 (definition), 164, 171/172, 176, 177 and 184 tell about Penumbra...<br /> <br /> Almost 99% the same as in W20... but no mentioning on any of them even hints that doors or ANY other thing might not being openable.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the hint, but either I did skip over it accidently or it is somewhere else, if anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T10:26:47-08:00","id":772396,"title":"","content":"Having never heard of something like this in Werewolf, the closet thing I can think of is something similar happening in Wraith. Maybe that's where this rule started? From a Storyteller treating the middle Umbra in the same manner as the Dark Umbra? The middle Umbra though isn't necessarily a good reflection of the real world the way the Dark Umbra is. Whole buildings may or may not exist in the middle Umbra that are in the real world.<br /> I could however see doors in a really high Gauntlet building existing, just because the webs are so thick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T11:51:39-08:00","id":772432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/771820-doors-in-the-pen-umbra?p=772268#post772268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, what building are you in that even has doors in the penumbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>This. In the penumbra a lot of the buildings are shadows, stylized reflections made of spirit stuff. Things are not necessarily going to directly correspond, so a door blocking the Garou in the physical world might not be present on the other side of the Gauntlet. That having been said, what is stopping the Garou from smashing a spirit door apart just like its physical counterpart? Things in the umbra aren't made of invincible.<br /> <br /> Portals to other realms are a different animal entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-23-2015, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}